;; The scoped decode's one raw store, "(s.f! (+ this 856) f0-1)" (ERROR:
;; Failed store, op 30), is the wvehicle.gc method-220 class: the
;; decompiler prints a bare `+` on a basic-typed `this` where only `&+`
;; compiles ("Cannot do math on a" the type, same substitution
;; wvehicle.gc:503's own og:preserve-this note already documents). Offset
;; 856 is this file's own already-landed `water-height` field
;; (vehicle-h.gc); kept as the compile-only `&+` substitution rather than
;; rewritten to a named field access, matching the established minimal-fix
;; convention. rigid-body-object-method-69 and rigid-body-object-method-73
;; are both real dispatches through vehicle's own inheritance chain (69
;; lands above this rung, 73 is rigid-body-object's own landed base,
;; rigid-body-object.gc:328); neither is a zero slot.
;;
;; former vinit-rung hold text, kept for the record: Scoped decode against
;; this worktree's own config (--config-override allowed_objects
;; [vehicle-util], levels_extract false, ntsc_v1) proves the earlier
;; wall stale -- the corpus copy of this function failed type prop at op 34
;; (Unknown symbol: rigid-body-control), which is now fully defined and
